SELECT import_new_structured_page_v1('3cbdc749-e9c9-44f3-8330-ecc1e3b38cc8'::uuid, '59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7'::uuid, 'a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a4000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005'::uuid, '{"pageId": "e0420000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "bookPartId": "59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7", "pageNumber": 42, "sourceShowsPrintedPageLabel": true, "printedPageLabel": "42", "printedPageNumber": 42, "pdfPageNumber": 425, "sequenceIndex": 32, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "scanLanguages": ["en"], "reviewEvidence": {"englishTranscriptionComplete": true, "arabicTranscriptionComplete": false, "blockOrderChecked": true, "identifiersChecked": true, "scanCompared": true}, "structuralNodes": [], "blocks": [{"id": "f0420000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 0, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Virtues of Salaat", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}, {"id": "f0420100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 1, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "been said above, it must be clearly understood that we deserve the punishments that have been laid down for our commission of sins, but the All-embracing mercy of Allah overrides everything and knows no bounds.", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}, {"id": "f0420200-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 2, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "It was a habit with the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) to enquire from the companions, just after Fajr, if anybody had seen any dream. He would then interpret the dream as related to him. One day, after enquiring from others as usual, the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) himself narrated a long dream in which two men came and took him with them. Besides others he reported certain events which he happened to see in his dream. He said: \"I noticed the head of a person being crushed with a heavy stone. It was struck with such force that, after crushing the head, the stone rolled down over a long distance. The head would assume its normal shape by the time the stone was brought back for repeating the process. This continued incessantly. On inquiring from one of my companions, I was told that the person first learnt the Qur''an, but failed to practise upon it and also used to go to sleep without offering the fardh salaat.\" There is another similar narration, in which the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) is reported to have seen (in his dream) a group of people being treated likewise. Jibra-eel (Alayhis salaam) informed him on his query that those were the persons who used to neglect their salaat.", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}, {"id": "f0420300-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 3, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Mujahid (Rahmatullah alaih) says, \"Allah blesses the people who guard their salaat, just as He blessed Hadhrat Ibrahim (Alayhis salaam) and his descendants.\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}, {"id": "f0420400-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 4, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Anas (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"If a person dies with sincere Imaan, observing the commandments of Allah, performing salaat, and paying Zakaat, when he dies Allah is pleased with him.\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}, {"id": "f0420500-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 5, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Anas (Radhiyallaho anho) also narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"Allah says, ''I hold back retribution, deserved by a locality, when I see therein some people who frequently visit the musjid, love one another for My sake, and pray for forgiveness in the hours of darkness.''\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}, {"id": "f0420600-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 6, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Abu Darda (Radhiyallaho anho) wrote to Hadhrat Salmaan: \"Spend most of your time in the musjid. I have heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, ''The musjid is the abode of the pious. Allah has taken upon Himself to bless the person who spends most of", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}]}'::jsonb);